From 35043e9f7b9e2a4a921cbaec11ad8bf4dc50fbe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Morten Stenshorne <mstensho@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:02:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Skip layout of fieldset children if display-locked.

Original change's description:
> Skip layout of fieldset children if display-locked.
>
> BlockNode::FirstChild() doesn't return any children if display-locked,
> but fieldsets are special and use GetFieldsetContent() and
> GetRenderedLegend() instead of that. Add guards.
>
> We *could* add a guard before attempting child layout in the fieldset
> algorithm, too, but that would suggest that all algorithms would have to
> worry about this, which isn't necessary. See crrev.com/c/8831561
>
> Bug: 589815787
> Change-Id: I226ecd64ec739f9478bb0693b346a9cb64633ed9
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8852595
